#
# Provides the HSL struct representing a color in the Hue-Saturation-Lightness
# color space. HSL is a cylindrical representation where hue is an angle on the
# color wheel (0-360 degrees), saturation measures color intensity (0.0-1.0),
# and lightness measures brightness from black (0.0) through pure color (0.5)
# to white (1.0). HSL is particularly useful for palette generation because
# hue rotation produces harmonious color schemes.
#
# This program is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify
# it under the terms of the GNU General Public License as published by
# the Free Software Foundation, either version 3 of the License, or
# any later version.
#
